[[4818,1815,"There is no adequate signage to warn visitors of the risk of drowning by entering the water at Sgwd Gwladys","drowning at Sgwd Gwladys",""],[4819,1815,"Existing signage in 'Waterfall Country' is overloaded with a variety of information, which although helpful for walking routes etc, is not explicit in warning of the real danger of death from entering the water","overloaded signage",""],[4820,1815,"Any sign(s) erected ought to be easily visible, in plain English and spell out the risk of death by drowning","inadequate signage",""],[4821,1815,"It is very unclear who bears responsibility for this particular area, which borders 3 local authority areas, and falls within the National Park and NRW jurisdiction","responsibility ambiguity",""],[9478,3614,"The signage at ALL waterfalls in 'Waterfall Country' must be addressed","lack of signage at waterfalls",""],[9479,3614,"Akeem Roden was not a strong swimmer and there were no adequate signs at the point he jumped in to warn him of the potential dangers and that he might drown","inadequate warning signs",""],[9480,3614,"Signage at each waterfall should be in plain, bold, easily understandable English, spelling out the danger of the power of the water","inadequate signage",""],[9481,3614,"Existing signage is overloaded with information and not present at the point where individuals may decide to enter the water","overloaded signage",""]]